\details{
\code{type} selects the quantity returned:
\itemize{
\item \code{"response"} (default): draws from the posterior predictive
distribution on the outcome scale, from
\code{\link[=posterior_predict.mvgam]{posterior_predict.mvgam()}}.
\item \code{"link"}: the linear predictor on the link scale, from
\code{\link[=posterior_linpred.mvgam]{posterior_linpred.mvgam()}}.
\item \code{"expected"}: the expectation E[Y | X] on the response
scale, from \code{\link[=posterior_epred.mvgam]{posterior_epred.mvgam()}}.
\item \code{"variance"}: the conditional variance Var[Y | theta] per
draw, from the family's mean-variance relation. It covers the
gaussian, student, lognormal, poisson, bernoulli, binomial,
negbinomial, gamma and beta families. Other families raise an
error. By default the variance is the observation noise around
the mean of the two submodels. \code{process_error = TRUE} also
conditions on each draw's sampled trend innovation.
\item \code{"terms"}: refused with a pointer to the functions that
decompose a prediction. \code{\link[=posterior_smooths.mvgam]{posterior_smooths.mvgam()}} returns
per-smooth draws. \code{\link[=fixef.mvgam]{fixef.mvgam()}} and \code{\link[=ranef.mvgam]{ranef.mvgam()}} return the
parametric and random-effect components.
\item \code{"latent_state"}: for closure-unit families, the posterior of
the latent state of each closure unit given its detection
history:
\itemize{
\item \code{nmix()}: the latent abundance \code{N} given the observed
visit counts (Royle 2004).
\item \code{occ()}: the occupancy probability \code{P(z = 1 | y_g)}.
}
\item \code{"detection"}: for \code{nmix()} and \code{occ()}, the per-visit
detection probability \eqn{p_{g,j}} on the response scale.
}
